# nredf: your machine-local bash aliases.
#
# Sourced whenever bash loads aliases (interactive shells). chezmoi seeded
# this file once, empty, and will never overwrite it again (the `create_`
# attribute) — edit it freely. Zsh has its own separate copy at
# ~/.config/zsh/aliases; this one is bash-only.
#
# Example:
#   alias ll="ls -la"
#
# For a simple alias shared across every shell, ~/.config/nredf/local.yaml
# is usually less to write — see ~/.config/nredf/README.md.
